The second half began from a failure. Methods that judge a label by its neighbors usually made models worse on standard representations. On a given dataset, most features of a general-purpose representation do not vary or do not relate to the property, and a distance counts them all (Chapter~\ref{chap:flaws}). The adaptive hybrid representation instead selects features for the task, from several representations, under a budget in features. \textbf{[RESULT NEEDED: one sentence, what Chapter~\ref{chap:method} found.]} \textbf{[RESULT NEEDED: one sentence, what Chapter~\ref{chap:similarity} found.]}

