Both halves lead to the same advice. Before choosing a model, a representation or a method for learning with noisy labels, ask where the labels came from and what shape their noise is likely to have. Then choose the features for the task, rather than taking one representation whole. No single choice was best on every dataset, so the choices that vary by dataset should be searched and compared fairly.

% CODE INPUT
