This matters in practice because representations keep changing. A new foundation model appears every few months in molecular, protein and antibody modeling. With the hybrid search, a researcher does not need to decide whether to replace their current representation or retrain their pipeline. They compute the new model's embeddings, add them to the representations searched, and re-run the search. The search then decides whether the new embedding contributes features, and if so, how many and which. The choice of representation is often set by familiarity or lab convention. The search replaces that choice with one measured on each task, and it can be repeated as new representations appear.


