The two cancer datasets use data from The Cancer Genome Atlas \citep{Weinstein2013}, downloaded through UCSC Xena \citep{Goldman2020}. Expression is read from each cohort's Illumina HiSeq RNA-seq matrix on the Xena TCGA hub (version 2017-10-13). It holds 20,530 genes as $\log_2(x+1)$ of the RSEM-normalized count \citep{Li2011RSEM} from the UNC RNA-seq pipeline. The same 20,530 genes appear in every cohort, and no gene filter is applied. Only primary tumors are kept (sample-type code 01 in the TCGA barcode). Barcodes are cut to the sample level, which leaves one sample per patient. Missing expression values are set to 0. There is no batch correction. Every fold holds out whole tissue source sites. A correction fitted on the training sites has no parameter for a site it never saw. A correction fitted on all sites has already seen the test samples.

