% TODO: review, needs manual review
\paragraph{Breast cancer PAM50 subtype.} The label is the PAM50 subtype call \citep{Parker2009} from the breast cancer clinical matrix on Xena \citep{TCGA2012BRCA}. Four classes are kept: luminal A, luminal B, basal-like and HER2-enriched. Tumors called normal-like, and tumors without a call, are dropped. Of 1,097 primary tumors with expression data, 821 remain: 421 luminal A, 192 luminal B, 141 basal-like and 67 HER2-enriched, from 19 tissue source sites.
